{% doc %}Editorial buying context below the existing interactive model comparison.{% enddoc %}
<section class="pq pq-buying-guide" aria-labelledby="CompareBuying-{{ section.id }}">
  <h2 class="pq-buying-guide__heading" id="CompareBuying-{{ section.id }}">Choosing an electric dirt bike alternative</h2>
  <div class="pq-buying-guide__columns">
    <div><h3>Start with the bike you need</h3><p>When considering a Sur-Ron alternative, compare riding purpose, fit and ownership support before choosing by peak power. A lower-priced bike may have less battery energy, different suspension, different dimensions or a smaller parts network. Similar headline specifications do not establish equal riding performance.</p></div>
    <div><h3>Compare the complete battery system</h3><p>Voltage and amp-hours describe different things. Nominal watt-hours are voltage multiplied by amp-hours. More nominal energy does not guarantee a particular riding distance: speed, rider weight, terrain and temperature all matter. Check whether charging figures describe the same starting and ending battery percentages.</p></div>
    <div><h3>Match the comparison to your budget</h3><p>Compare the exact configuration and the total price for your destination, including taxes and duties. The <a href="{{ collections['electric-dirt-bikes'].url | default: '/collections/electric-dirt-bikes' }}">Panquire electric dirt bike collection</a> shows the current T-01 and T-02 offers together. Use each manufacturer's source link above to check competitor prices and specifications.</p></div>
    <div><h3>Keep claimed and tested results separate</h3><p>The tables use published manufacturer specifications. They are not a head-to-head acceleration, handling or range test. Compare range conditions and weight definitions before drawing conclusions. Ask about compatible parts, warranty scope and service arrangements for the model and destination you choose.</p></div>
  </div>
  <h2 class="pq-buying-guide__heading">T-01 or T-02?</h2>
  <p>T-01 is Panquire's lower-priced 60V option. T-02 uses a 72V battery with more nominal energy and a higher stated peak output. Review the current figures below, then visit the product page for fit, charging and ownership details.</p>
  {% render 'pq-dirt-bike-selection' %}
  <div class="pq-buying-guide__links"><a href="{{ all_products['t-01'].url }}">Explore the T-01</a><a href="{{ all_products['t-02'].url }}">Explore the T-02</a><a href="{{ pages.contact.url | default: '/pages/contact' }}">Ask a comparison question</a></div>
</section>
